Binding scaffold for reticulum-go-protocols
==========================================

Use this file to add a new language binding under bindings/<lang>/.
It is language-neutral. Follow an existing binding for idioms.

Integration paths
-----------------

librrc (in-process RRC hub/client)
  - Link or load the shared library built by task build-librrc
  - Authoritative C ABI: include/rrc.h
  - Artifacts: bin/librrc.so (Linux), bin/librrc.dylib, bin/librrc.dll

libmf (MF packet codec)
  - task build-libmf
  - include/mf.h

liblxmf (LXMF message codec)
  - task build-liblxmf
  - include/lxmf.h

Reference bindings already in tree
----------------------------------

  bindings/python  librrc + libmf + liblxmf (ctypes)
  bindings/rust    librrc wrappers (safe Rust over extern)
  bindings/java    librrc wrappers (JNA)
  bindings/lua     librrc wrappers (LuaJIT FFI)
  bindings/c       librrc + libmf direct C examples
  bindings/cpp     librrc + libmf CMake smoke tests

Each RRC binding keeps demos under bindings/<lang>/examples/{smoke,codec-roundtrip,hub-client}.

Suggested directory layout
--------------------------

  bindings/<lang>/
    Makefile or native build file
    <package>/ or src/
      raw ABI layer (thin)
      errors
      types / constants
      envelope (codec)
      identity
      node
      hub
      client
      event
      util (string and buffer helpers)
    tests/
    examples/

librrc module map (required surface)
------------------------------------

Mirror these C entry points. Names may be idiomatic in the host language.
Handles are opaque uint64. Destroy before process exit.

Version and errors
  rrc_version
  rrc_last_error
  RRC_API_VERSION string must match the header you compiled or loaded against
  Error codes: OK, INVALID_ARG, INVALID_HANDLE, NOT_FOUND, STATE, IO,
  INTERNAL, TIMEOUT, TRUNCATED

Envelope codec
  rrc_envelope_create / set_room / set_nick / set_body_text / set_destination
  rrc_envelope_get_* / marshal / unmarshal / destroy
  rrc_normalize_room / rrc_sanitize_nick

Node
  rrc_node_create (empty config path means in-memory defaults)
  rrc_node_start / rrc_node_stop / rrc_node_destroy
  rrc_node_set_identity
  rrc_node_add_udp_interface
  rrc_node_has_path

Identity
  rrc_identity_generate / load / save / destroy / hash
  rrc_identity_seed_destination

Hub
  rrc_hub_create / start / announce / hash / peer_count / destroy
  rrc_hub_event_poll

Client
  rrc_client_dial / join / part / send_msg / send_notice / send_action / ping
  rrc_client_close / rrc_client_event_poll

Event kinds
  WELCOME, JOINED, PARTED, MSG, NOTICE, ACTION, ERROR, PONG
  HELLO, JOIN, PART, CLOSE, TIMEOUT

Tests to include
----------------

Minimum
  version string non-empty and matches RRC_API_VERSION
  envelope create / marshal / unmarshal round-trip
  node create / start / stop / destroy
  identity generate and hash length 16
  normalize_room and sanitize_nick

Stronger
  hub-client example over local UDP loopback
  client dial / join / send_msg / event poll
  wait for rrc_node_has_path before dial

Codec bindings (mf/lxmf)
  round-trip pack/unpack in unit tests
  examples: bindings/python/examples/lxmf-roundtrip, bindings/c/examples/{mf,lxmf}-smoke
  CI via scripts/ci/run-codec-bindings.sh

Build and smoke
---------------

From repository root:

  task build-bindings
  make -C bindings/<lang> test
  make -C bindings/<lang> examples

Wire CI using scripts/ci/run-<lang>-bindings.sh.
Hub-client live mesh: scripts/ci/run-hub-client-bindings.sh.

